# A source file carrying a stray control byte reads as binary to git, and a
# binary file has no three-way merge: two branches that both edit it do not
# conflict cleanly — one side is kept whole and the other's edits are dropped,
# with nothing in the merge output to say so. That is the shape of trap
# `packages/plugin-flock/src/client/index.ts` was, holding a literal NUL as a
# watch-key separator until it was written as an escape instead.
#
# `diff` below forces a textual diff whatever bytes a file holds, so such a
# file can never again review as "Bin 24493 -> 25169 bytes" with its real
# change unreadable. It cannot save the merge — git's own binary detection
# decides that and no attribute overrides it — so the guard that matters is
# `packages/architecture-checks/src/source-nul-bytes.test.ts`, which keeps the
# byte out of the tree in the first place.
*.ts text diff
*.tsx text diff
*.vue text diff
*.css text diff
*.md text diff
*.json text diff
*.jsonc text diff
*.html text diff
